  },
  {
    rank: '03',
    tone: 'violet',
    scale: 'Scalable with a business layer',
    title: 'B.Tech Biotechnology, Food Technology or Pharmaceutical Engineering',
    gate: 'The Andhra Pradesh 2026 BiPC notice lists B.E/B.Tech in Bio-Technology, Food Technology, Food Engineering, Agricultural Engineering and Pharmaceutical Engineering. Its eligibility line asks for Botany, Zoology, Physics and Chemistry, not Maths.',
    pay: 'No sourced range is used here. Pay depends on the college, the plant or lab and your skills, so ask for last year\'s placement list.',
    when: 'Pay moves on a plant, quality or process role after a few years, or when you add a data or regulatory skill.',
    reason: 'Process, quality and testing skills travel across employers and can become consulting or a testing service.',
    layer: 'Quality and compliance consulting for small food or pharma units, or a testing lab once the licence rules are met.',
    watch: 'A B.Tech label does not guarantee a campus job. Check the placement denominator, not only the brochure median.',
  },
  {
    rank: '04',
    tone: 'teal',
    scale: 'Scalable with a business layer',
    title: 'BSc Nursing, with the abroad route in view',
    gate: 'Class 12 with Physics, Chemistry, Biology and English. Admission routes differ by state, and some seats use NEET UG scores, so read your state\'s notice and confirm the college is approved by the nursing council.',
