        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">An illustration, not a real fee. The rest of the budget should still pay for living costs, books, a laptop and internet, a short skill course, and a reserve for a second attempt or a bridge year.</p>

  <ul>
    <li>Count the full course: tuition, hostel, lab and clinical fees, exam fees and uniforms, for every year.</li>
    <li>Go above the benchmark only for an edge you cannot copy cheaply, such as hospital access, council approval and placement names you have checked yourself.</li>
    <li>For MBBS, the NMC told colleges in April 2026 to charge fees only for the 4.5 years of study, so ask a private college for its full fee in writing.</li>
    <li>A loan is repaid from your salary, and your salary depends on the skill you added, not on the fee you paid. Borrow only when the licence needs the degree by law. This is general information, not financial advice; get loan terms in writing.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="stream">Still in Class 11? Test BiPC before you lean on it</h2>

  <p>
    If you have not locked the stream, test the interest first. Biology-heavy routes mean long training, competitive seats and slow early pay.
  </p>

  <div class="comparison-grid">
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--teal">
      <div class="compare-card__label">BiPC fits when</div>
      <ul>
        <li>You are drawn to biology, healthcare or life-science work, and you can accept long training and slow early pay.</li>
        <li>You have a second route written down, such as pharmacy, nursing or a life-science BSc with a data skill.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--gold">
      <div class="compare-card__label">PCM fits when</div>
      <ul>
        <li>You can sustain Maths and have no biology-only goal. PCM keeps computer science, data and most engineering open.</li>
        <li>PCM closes medicine, dentistry, veterinary and some life-science routes, so it is a trade and not a free upgrade.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    Choose by interest, ability, cost, time to income and a backup, plus the skills you can build beside the stream.
  </p>

